Fix exclusive constraints on tuple properties (#3573)

# `UNLESS CONFLICT ON` fails in `FOR` statement · Issue #2295 · edgedb/edgedb
created: 2021-03-01, last updated: 2025-01-04, [Read more](https://github.com/edgedb/edgedb/issues/2295)

type Movie {
required property title -> str;
required link director -> Person;
type Person {
required property name -> str {
constraint exclusive;
};
...
This behavior is maybe unfortunate but is intended and documented: https://www.edgedb.com/docs/edgeql/statements/insert
A caveat, however, is that UNLESS CONFLICT will not prevent conflicts caused between multiple DML operations in the same query; inserting two conflicting objects (through use of FOR or simply with two INSERT statements) will cause a constraint error.
...
In the example case, you should be able to fix it by lifting up the nested insert outside the FOR statement using WITH.

